working_notes/claim_ledger.md:315:## Claim: TV-separable payoff-weighted reward measures give common domination
working_notes/claim_ledger.md:319:Evidence: Choose a countable TV-dense set \(\{\nu_n\}\) and define \(\lambda=\sum_n2^{-n}\nu_n\) for each \((t,a)\), or combine over finite \(a\in G\). If \(\lambda(B)=0\), then every \(\nu_n(B)=0\); total-variation approximation implies every \(\mu^\theta_{t,a}(B)=0\). Thus the reward-measure domination theorem applies. Compact metric parameter classes with TV-continuous \(\theta\mapsto\mu^\theta_{t,a}\) satisfy this separability condition.
