working_notes/failed_attempts.md:85:Attempt: Prove a finite-action minimax identity while keeping \(V_\theta=\sup_{a\in[0,1]}\sum_t\mathbb E_\theta r_t(a)\) or a continuum Bayes envelope in the displayed \(\Psi\).
working_notes/failed_attempts.md:87:Lesson: Every finite-grid theorem must consistently restrict learner actions, comparator values, and posterior Bayes envelopes to \(G\). Continuum statements require a separate discretization lemma.
